# Bytecode must never enter an image. Two reasons, and the second one bit us:
# stale .pyc can shadow source that was legitimately removed, and a .pyc holds
# its string literals in plain, greppable form — so shipping __pycache__ leaked
# every licensed prompt out of a customer image whose .py had been stripped
# (measured 2026-08-28: prompts.cpython-312.pyc was present and readable in a
# container built with BRAIN_SHIP_PROMPTS=0).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

.git/
.pytest_cache/
_gate_logs/
tests/
rig/
scripts/
docs/
*.md
.env
.env.*
